d entry for the fix.\n\n**CI:**\n- `ci-0001` on the fix commit: passed.\n- The first PR attempt was rejected because `main` had moved since I branched, so I merged the latest `main` into the branch, verified the fix was still intact, and re-ran CI \u2014 `ci-0002` on the merged commit `a5f9b0ab08` also passed.\n\n**Pull request:** [#101](https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101) is open against `main` with alex requested as reviewer. Per policy, I did not merge it \u2014 that's for the code owner to approve.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking at the repository and the relevant files.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Wik7yDoHPyqu5ZxBFPgG2d", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_files", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VkAwVSTc34B5e14kpbmxqu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01FpLoZZToQKXRU1djTAQ4EN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012ezdL3jD29rmm35FrCoQZo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "CHANGELOG.md"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `round_money` imports and uses `ROUND_HALF_UP` even though the docstring (and FIN-212) call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. I'll create a branch and fix it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01WEK3vjw4K9QVpeeXZrpTUp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01RRc38X